.TH "DEDB DOWNLOADGOG" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.14" "dedb downloadgog Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-downloadgog \- Download and extract DOSBox-based owned games from GOG.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb downloadgog
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download and extract DOSBox-based owned games from GOG.
.PP
Pass --game for a single game, or --all for every owned game
classified as DOSBox-based (see `lsgog`).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fP
Keep the installer/ directory after extracting.
.TP
\fB\-\-game\fP TEXT
Download only this game id.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fP
Download every owned game classified as DOSBox-based.
.TP
\fB\-r,\fP \-\-refreshmetadata
Re-fetch GOG dependency metadata instead of using the cached copy.
.TP
\fB\-\-redownload\fP
Re-download and re-extract games even if they're already downloaded.
.TP
\fB\-\-merge\-save\fP / \-\-no\-merge\-save
--no-merge-save: leave bundled save files under game/__support/save/ instead of copying them onto the game root the way GOG's installer would.
